[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4088503737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117604#issuecomment-4088503737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117604","id":4088503737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zsZ25","user":{"login":"dinklydoo","id":178973793,"node_id":"U_kgDOCqrsYQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178973793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo","html_url":"https://github.com/dinklydoo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinklydoo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T08:13:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T08:13:20Z","body":"Looks like a texture repeat issue, I get expected black when the texel is at index 1 ( ~vec2(0.00199) ) so 0 must be wrapping around to white with linear interpolation which gives gray and vice versa for white. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4088503737/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4089390951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117604#issuecomment-4089390951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117604","id":4089390951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zvydn","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T11:11:25Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T11:11:25Z","body":"> e.g. with a ramp that goes from black @ 0.0 to white @ 1.0, when inputting 0.0 as the UV into texture(), the colour returned is white, not black as it should be.\n\nThe returned color is grey, not white. This is expected result given a combination of linear texture filter and enabled texture repeat.\n\nSetting either `filter_nereast` or `repeat_disabled` hint for the sampled texture is enough to make sampling at `0.0` return black.\n\n<img width=\"1238\" height=\"712\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0451d9ce-ae27-46d0-b083-703c1888f26f\" />|<img width=\"1238\" height=\"712\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5faff53-d498-4676-8844-07ee785a9776\" />|<img width=\"1238\" height=\"712\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eee807a3-4a40-4fe9-a814-efd31ab8d958\" />\n-|-|-\n\nInterestingly, sampling at `1.0` with `filter_nereast` (and repeat enabled, by default) results in black color for me (got the same result for d3d12/vulkan/opengl). I suspect this may vary between GPUs/drivers though?\n\n<img width=\"1238\" height=\"712\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c213a59-0917-471c-96e8-3819cb57ea12\" />|<img width=\"1238\" height=\"712\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/09d7ab76-0d82-4a28-9812-acc6501137d2\" />|<img width=\"1238\" height=\"712\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cdaff6b0-2559-40a4-96f1-254191c4962f\" />\n-|-|-\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21924.61) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600G with Radeon Graphics (12 threads) - 31.29 GiB memory","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4089390951/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]